From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] vd_lavc: add v4l2request to the hwdec auto-probe whitelist

The v4l2request hwdecs (V4L2 stateless decoders through FFmpeg's V4L2
Request API hwaccels) are not in hwdec_autoprobe_info, so --hwdec=auto,
auto-safe, yes and auto-copy never try them; only auto-unsafe does, and
then last. Players that ask libmpv for "auto" or "auto-copy" (most GUI
front ends) therefore fall back to software decoding on SoCs whose only
video decoders are stateless (Rockchip RK3588/RK3399, Allwinner, NXP
i.MX8M, MediaTek, Raspberry Pi 5 HEVC), even when the decoder is there.

v4l2request is as safe to probe as drm:
- the hwaccel only binds to a decoder that it has probed: the media
  device's video node must list the codec's OUTPUT pixel format and the
  stream's frame size (VIDIOC_ENUM_FMT/ENUM_FRAMESIZES). Otherwise frames
  context creation fails, get_format_hwdec() sets hwdec_failed and mpv
  moves on to the next hwdec or software, as for any other failing hwdec;
- frames are DRM PRIME dmabufs, imported by the same drmprime interop as
  --hwdec=drm, or downloaded with av_hwframe_transfer_data() for -copy;
- on systems without V4L2 stateless decoders it is never selected.

Place it right after drm (and v4l2request-copy after drm-copy), i.e.
after vaapi/nvdec/vulkan, so systems with a native GPU decoder behave
exactly as before.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 DOCS/interface-changes/hwdec-v4l2request-auto.txt | 1 +
 DOCS/man/options.rst                              | 4 ++++
 video/decode/vd_lavc.c                            | 2 ++
 3 files changed, 7 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 DOCS/interface-changes/hwdec-v4l2request-auto.txt

diff --git a/DOCS/interface-changes/hwdec-v4l2request-auto.txt b/DOCS/interface-changes/hwdec-v4l2request-auto.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2c156ba
--- /dev/null
+++ b/DOCS/interface-changes/hwdec-v4l2request-auto.txt
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+add `v4l2request` and `v4l2request-copy` to the hwdecs that `--hwdec=auto` and `--hwdec=auto-copy` try
diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
index fa71dc0..a850ea0 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -1371,6 +1371,10 @@ Video
     :nvdec-copy: copies video back to system RAM (Any platform CUDA is available)
     :drm:       requires ``--vo=gpu`` or ``--vo=gpu-next`` (Linux only)
     :drm-copy:   copies video back to system RAM (Linux only)
+    :v4l2request: requires ``--vo=gpu``, ``--vo=gpu-next`` or ``--vo=dmabuf-wayland``
+                  (Linux with V4L2 stateless decoders, e.g. Rockchip, Allwinner,
+                  MediaTek, NXP; needs an FFmpeg with the V4L2 Request API hwaccels)
+    :v4l2request-copy: copies video back to system RAM (Linux only)
     :vulkan:    requires ``--vo=gpu-next`` (Any platform with Vulkan Video Decoding)
     :vulkan-copy: copies video back to system RAM (Any platform with Vulkan Video Decoding)
 
diff --git a/video/decode/vd_lavc.c b/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
index 399e1d5..75a29aa 100644
--- a/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
+++ b/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
@@ -270,6 +270,7 @@ const struct autoprobe_info hwdec_autoprobe_info[] = {
     {"vaapi",           HWDEC_FLAG_AUTO | HWDEC_FLAG_WHITELIST},
     {"vdpau",           HWDEC_FLAG_AUTO},
     {"drm",             HWDEC_FLAG_AUTO | HWDEC_FLAG_WHITELIST},
+    {"v4l2request",     HWDEC_FLAG_AUTO | HWDEC_FLAG_WHITELIST},
     {"mediacodec",      HWDEC_FLAG_AUTO},
     {"videotoolbox",    HWDEC_FLAG_AUTO | HWDEC_FLAG_WHITELIST},
     {"d3d11va-copy",    HWDEC_FLAG_AUTO | HWDEC_FLAG_WHITELIST},
@@ -279,6 +280,7 @@ const struct autoprobe_info hwdec_autoprobe_info[] = {
     {"vaapi-copy",      HWDEC_FLAG_AUTO | HWDEC_FLAG_WHITELIST},
     {"vdpau-copy",      HWDEC_FLAG_AUTO | HWDEC_FLAG_WHITELIST},
     {"drm-copy",        HWDEC_FLAG_AUTO | HWDEC_FLAG_WHITELIST},
+    {"v4l2request-copy", HWDEC_FLAG_AUTO | HWDEC_FLAG_WHITELIST},
     {"mediacodec-copy", HWDEC_FLAG_AUTO | HWDEC_FLAG_WHITELIST},
     {"videotoolbox-copy", HWDEC_FLAG_AUTO | HWDEC_FLAG_WHITELIST},
     {0}
